  "description": "Sharqiyah Desalination Company SAOG (SDC) owns, operates, and maintains the Sur Independent Water Plant in Al-Bar, Sur, supplying potable water across Oman's Sharqiyah region on a Build-Own-Operate (BOO) basis. Established in January 2007 and listed on MSX in June 2013, the company operates a seawater reverse osmosis (RO) desalination plant utilizing a large beachwell intake catchment, expanded from 17.66 MIGD to an aggregate contracted capacity of 29 MIGD (131,837 m3/day). Under its Amended and Restated Water Purchase Agreement expiring in March 2036, 100% of the plant's water capacity and output is sold to sole offtaker Nama Power and Water Procurement Company (NPWP).",
